Description:
The Bachelor of Arts in Music, Composition track is designed for students who demonstrate a strong creative ability in the composition of original music and who are interested in pursuing composition as a profession or as a foundation for a related music career or graduate study. The curriculum provides a strong foundation in music theory, music history, and performance, with a special emphasis on the techniques and practices of music composition.

### Program Goals

- To develop a high degree of musicianship, including:

- aural and sight-singing skills;
- keyboard proficiency;
- an understanding of the common elements and organizational patterns of music and their interaction;

- To develop an understanding of the cultural and historical contexts of music.

- To develop the ability to perform with proficiency on a primary instrument or voice.

- To develop skills in composing, including:

- the ability to write music in a variety of styles, for a variety of media;
- the ability to work with both acoustic and electronic media; and
- an acquaintance with a large body of contemporary repertoire.

- To develop the ability to write and speak about music intelligently.
